### 21.2 Trust-Gated Discount Sustainability

**Concern:** 50% discount for trust score 80+ agents could erode revenue.

**Analysis:** Trust-gated discounts are applied to the BASE credit cost, not protocol fees.
The 2-credit orchestration fee is fixed regardless of trust tier.
Discounts apply to skill invocation costs (which go to skill creators, not protocol).

```
Example: Agent calls a 10-credit skill (using canonical 5-tier boundaries)

new    (0-19,  base price):  Agent pays 10cr   → 8.5cr creator, 1.5cr protocol
building(20-39, base price): Agent pays 10cr   → 8.5cr creator, 1.5cr protocol
caution(40-59, 10% off):     Agent pays 9cr    → 7.65cr creator, 1.35cr protocol
standard(60-79, 20% off):    Agent pays 8cr    → 6.8cr creator, 1.2cr protocol
trusted(80-89, 25% off):     Agent pays 7.5cr  → 6.375cr creator, 1.125cr protocol
proceed(90+ AND verified AND 6mo AND $50 rev, 30% off):
                              Agent pays 7cr    → 5.95cr creator, 1.05cr protocol

Protocol always earns: orchestration fee (2cr) + 15% of skill cost
High-trust agents pay less BUT transact MORE (volume compensates margin)
```

**Key insight:** The discount incentivizes agents to BUILD trust, which increases
platform usage volume. A 50% discount with 3x volume = 50% more total revenue.

### 21.3 Gas Cost Budget

Direct EIP-3009 settlement requires the server to pay gas.

```
Base L2 gas costs (March 2026, verified against BaseScan):
  EIP-3009 receiveWithAuthorization: ~65,000 gas
  Base L2 minimum gas price: 0.005 gwei (Jovian upgrade floor, not 0.001)
  L2 execution per tx: 65,000 × 0.005 gwei ≈ 0.000000325 ETH
  L1 data fee (security): typically equals or exceeds L2 execution
  Total cost per settlement: ~$0.001 (at ETH ~$2,000, including L1 fees)

  Daily budget at 10,000 tx/day:
    Immediate (each tx):  10,000 × $0.001 = $10.00/day = $300/month
    Batched (hourly):     ~240 batch txs × $0.001 = $0.24/day = $7/month
    Deferred (daily):     ~500 agent settlements × $0.001 = $0.50/day = $15/month
    Mixed (realistic):    70% batched + 25% immediate + 5% deferred ≈ $100/month

  Gas funded from: hot wallet (existing EVM_PRIVATE_KEY)
  Keep ~0.05 ETH on Base (~$100, lasts 1-3 months)
  Alert threshold: < 0.01 ETH on Base
```

Gas costs are low but not negligible at scale. Batched settlement is 40x cheaper per tx.

**AID vs x402 facilitator cost comparison (verified — Coinbase charges $0.001/tx
since January 2026, after 1,000 free tx/month):**
```
At 10K tx/month:  x402 = $9/mo (1K free + 9K × $0.001)  |  AID batched = $7/mo
At 50K tx/month:  x402 = $49/mo                          |  AID batched = $36/mo
At 100K tx/month: x402 = $99/mo                          |  AID batched = $72/mo
```
AID is cheaper at every volume level when batched settlement is used.

